  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 18-1432, Nasrallah versus Barr. Mr. Hughes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As the government says, \"a grant of withholding or deferral leaves the final order of removal undisturbed.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress enacted the jurisdiction-stripping provision in (2)(C), it expressly defined the key term \"order of removal.\" It is an order that finds an individual deportable or orders deportation. A CAT order does neither, and the government does not disagree. CAT relief is temporary, applicable only to the country where an individual is likely to be tortured or killed. If CAT relief is granted, the removal order remains enforceable. As the government says, \"a grant of withholding or deferral leaves the final order of removal undisturbed.\" When Congress enacted (2)(C), it also stripped jurisdiction of expedited removal"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Do you agree -- MR. HUGHES: That's both -- JUSTICE GINSBURG: -- do you agree that, assuming that review of the -- of BIA fact-finding, assuming that it's available, wouldn't that review be highly deferential to the BIA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So why does it encompass statutory withholding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Why does it necessarily encompass statutory withholding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Like cancellation of removal, things like that affect that Act?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUGHES: Yes, Your Honor. The only things that I'm aware of that do not fall -- that are not swept within that are CAT relief, CAT withholding, and CAT deferral, and, as Your Honor points out --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Can I just ask you before your time expires -- and I -- I'd like the government to answer this too -- what you have to say about -- putting aside the question of waiver, about the Eleventh Circuit's holding that the criminal alien bar applies at all in this case, since the ground for removal in this case is 1227(a)(2)(A)(i), right, not --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I ask you a --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: We pledged -- we pledged to our treaty partners that we would not return a person to a place where the returnee would be likely subject to torture."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government made about the notion that the removal order is limited to removal only to the country specified in the removal order. Respectfully, that's just legally wrong. The regulation is 8 CFR 1240.12, subprovision (d). It does state that an immigration judge needs to identify one or more countries to which removal is to occur."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is just curiosity to me. Can the government change a port of deportation? Assuming a prisoner comes and says, my mother is in this other country, I'd rather go there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3b37827b5b2e60a8974e9b7acee80ff4c1bbc43192fac2fe135df912d0240a2e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3b37827b5b2e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do they have to go back to the judge to get permission to do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1432",
      "confidence": 0.0,
